    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 11 slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear offensive anchor, sporting an elite 80.65 efficiency score against Rocker. With an xwOBA of .469, **Yordan Alvarez** is positioned to thrive, supported by a favorable matchup and an advantageous spot in the two-hole. Close behind is **Christian Yelich** (74.33), who benefits from a prime platoon edge against Chandler and an additional boost due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which significantly improves the probability of a stolen base\u2014a critical factor for our 5x5 strategy. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.78) also grades as a strong start, though his high-upside matchup against Lodolo carries a 39% rain risk that necessitates monitoring throughout the afternoon.\n\nWhile the core of the outfield remains productive, the middle infield remains competitive, leading to a tight decision on the bench. **Luke Raley** (44.02) was the final cut, narrowly missing the cut behind **Junior Caminero** (53.60); while **Luke Raley** holds a platoon advantage today, his raw efficiency remains below the threshold required to displace **Junior Caminero** in the utility spot, despite the latter facing a difficult matchup against Gilbert. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Carson Benge**, whose score dropped to a basement-level 32.80 due to a brutal matchup against the 1.50 xERA of Rivera, confirming his place on the bench to preserve our game caps.\n\nBeyond the matchup variables, the Zebras must navigate a few situational hurdles. Beyond the precipitation threats facing **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Lars Nootbaar**, our catchers face a mixed bag: **Gary Sanchez** (56.06) is a strong play against the high-xERA Chandler, whereas **Dillon Dingler** (46.92) is essentially a marginal start, held down by a tough matchup against the 2.84 xERA of S\u00e1nchez. We are keeping **Hyeseong Kim** and **Nelson Velazquez** sidelined as they remain outside of the active rotation, and we continue to monitor the development of depth pieces like **Colt Keith**, **Josh Smith**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** as we look to optimize our path to the league lead in stolen bases and counting stats.",
